# A call's local write does not change the callee's data: each leaf() starts from count 0 (the book «Локальное
# присваивание не меняет умолчание следующих вызовов»); the merged copy is no callable: its call refuses 5.
(
    Observed:
        int: first 0
        int: second 0
        int: third 0
        int: before 0
)
@: shared data[0]
fn: leaf () int (int: count 0)
    count := count + 1
    return: count
shared\Observed\first := leaf()
shared\Observed\second := leaf()
shared\Observed\third := leaf()
@: descriptor merge(leaf)
shared\Observed\before := descriptor\data\count
int: rejected descriptor()
